      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "XML::Parser versions through 2.47 for Perl has an off-by-one heap buffer overflow in st_serial_stack.  In the case (stackptr == stacksize - 1), the stack will NOT be expanded. Then the new value will be written at location (++stackptr), which equals stacksize and therefore falls just outside the allocated buffer.  The bug can be observed when parsing an XML file with very deep element nesting",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
